infographic compare-binary-horizontal-underline-text-vs
data
  title Liveness vs readiness: restart me vs route to me
  desc Confuse them and a DB blip restarts the fleet — dependency checks belong only in readiness
  compares
    - label Liveness — should I be restarted?
      children
        - label Asks: broken beyond self-repair?
          desc Deadlocked or wedged — the only state a restart can actually fix
        - label Fail: kubelet restarts the container
          desc Destroys process state; a restart never repairs a database
        - label Check ONLY what a restart fixes
          desc Never dependencies — a DB ping here turns a blip into a restart storm
        - label Threshold 3 x 10s = 30s before kill
          desc A 30s DB failover sits exactly on the kill line
    - label Readiness — should I get traffic now?
      children
        - label Asks: serviceable right now?
          desc Reversible and cheap — the right lever during outages and drains
        - label Fail: removed from Service endpoints
          desc Pod stays warm, keeps caches, rejoins when the dependency returns
        - label Check hard dependencies with a timeout
          desc The DB pool ping belongs here, not in liveness
        - label Threshold 2 x 5s = ~10s out of rotation
          desc Doubles as the drain flag: flip to 503 first on SIGTERM
theme
  palette #f43f5e #14b8a6
